> jaroslav - how often do you sync with linus ? i am wondering what the
> best approach is for maintaining my ALSA source base given that i am
> now building and running 2.5. i'd prefer to use ALSA CVS ...

for getting the latest version with 2.5, you can copy the files in
alsa-kernel directories to the corresponding places of 2.5 kernel
tree, such as,

	alsa-kernel/core -> linux-2.5.xx/sound/core
	alsa-kernel/include -> linux-2.5.xx/include/sound
	...


